+# Codex daily work-quota gate — 2026-09-22
+
+## Task
+Implement the master-goal rule "Codex is paid fallback only and must stay at or
+below 30 percent of daily AI-agent work, preferring Claude/OpenCode" as a real,
+repository-wide enforcement gate in the existing master-coordinator dispatch
+path, with focused regression tests. No production deployment.
+
+## Why
+The rule was documented but never enforced: Codex was only gated by explicit
+`allowPaid`/`--allow-paid` and per-call opt-in, with zero accounting of how much
+of a day's AI-agent work Codex actually performed. The authoritative daily work
+ledger (`state/ai-agent-reports.jsonl` - the shared log every agent already
+writes via reportAutomatedAgentResult/reportSelfExecuted/runSubtask) was not
+being read to guard paid fallback dispatches.
+
+## Current state
+Fresh worktree from `origin/master` @ `dd190cbf1b8a757a9bca0ae95faad5f2bdacf2d9`
+(17 commits ahead of local `master` at device). Inspected existing agent
+selection/guard code: `scripts/master-coordinator.cjs` (buildDefaultSubtasks,
+dispatchSubtask codex branch, summarizeMasterResults), `lib/agent-history.js`,
+`lib/agent-session-guard.js`, `data/desktop-ai-policy.json`. Verified no active
+PR or unmerged branch implements a Codex daily-work quota. `opencode/master-goal-agent-governance`
+covers CPU-load + process census (a separate slice) and is intentionally not
+duplicated here. `opencode/agent-work-quota-20260915` carries no unique commits.
+
+## Target state
+A Codex dispatch is refused with `CODEX_QUOTA_EXCEEDED` (never invoked, never
+written to the work ledger) whenever Codex is already above 30% of the trailing
+day's dispatched AI-agent work; exactly 30% remains allowed; Claude/OpenCode
+remain the preferred continuation (the planner's own OpenCode slice is not
+duplicated). The share is observable via `npm run codex:quota`.
+
+## Files / systems involved
+- `lib/codex-work-quota.js` (new): pure daily-share accounting over the shared
+  agent-report ledger; trailing-24h window; `done`/`failed` dispatched entries
+  count as work (assigned/queued do not); blocking is strict and falsifiable.
+- `scripts/master-coordinator.cjs`: quota gate in the PAID_FALLBACK branch of
+  `dispatchSubtask` (before any subprocess, configurable via
+  `opts.agentReportsPath`/`opts.quotaNow`/`opts.codexMaxDailyShare`, with an
+  `opts.invokeCodex` seam for deterministic tests); `CODEX_QUOTA_EXCEEDED`
+  added to the PENDING status set; blocked dispatches are excluded from
+  `reportAutomatedAgentResult` so they never corrupt the ledger's ratio.
+- `package.json`: new `codex:quota` script (read-only monitor).
+- `test/codex-work-quota.test.js` (new, 11 tests) +
+  `test/master-coordinator.test.js` (3 new gate tests).
+
+## Known risks
+- Strict boundary with no fudge floor: a day where the only work so far is
+  Codex (e.g. 1/1) blocks further Codex until other agents do work - this is
+  the literal rule, applied honestly.
+- The count is only as good as the shared ledger: agents that never report
+  into `state/ai-agent-reports.jsonl` are invisible, so the quota measures the
+  system's own recorded daily work.
+- Trailing 24h window (not UTC calendar day) avoids a midnight cliff splitting
+  one session across two accounting days; documented in the module.
+
+## Golden systems that must be preserved
+Master-coordinator routing/leases/resource gates; agent report schema
+(`state/ai-agent-reports.jsonl`); Codex explicit opt-in (`allowPaid`) and
+fail-closed behavior; session guard; one-task-one-PR; LKG/rollback; VNO.
+
+## Errors that must not return
+A quota-blocked Codex dispatch being invoked or written to the work ledger as
+`failed` (a real ratio corruption found and fixed during verification); a
+blocked Codex false-greening an overall PASS; over-blocking at a share below
+30%; the gate claiming a share from a ledger it never read.
+
+## Exact patch / change plan
+1. Add `lib/codex-work-quota.js` (read ledger, count dispatched work in window,
+   decide at `<=maxShare`).
+2. Gate `dispatchSubtask`'s Codex branch on the decision before spawning
+   Codex; return `CODEX_QUOTA_EXCEEDED` and skip `reportAutomatedAgentResult`.
+3. Register `CODEX_QUOTA_EXCEEDED` as PENDING in `summarizeMasterResults`.
+4. Add `codex:quota` npm script + inline CLI in the module.
+5. Add focused module tests and coordinator gate tests; run full `npm run check`.
+
+## Tests to run
+`node --test test/codex-work-quota.test.js test/master-coordinator.test.js`;
+`node scripts/check-js.js`; `npm run check`; `npm run desktop-ai:check`;
+`git diff --check`; `node lib/codex-work-quota.js` smoke.
+
+## Deployment / PR plan
+Branch `opencode/codex-work-quota-20260922` -> single review PR to `master`.
+No direct master push, auto-merge or production deployment. This patch touches
+no deployable app/api surface, so the existing Vercel quota guard should skip
+deployment of the slice itself.
+
+## Current progress
+Module, coordinator gate, npm script and all 14 focused tests are implemented
+and passing. Full repository `npm run check` remains to run before commit.
+
+## Next action
+Run full `npm run check` + `desktop-ai:check`; fix any regression; commit; push;
+open PR; report exact evidence incl. before/after PC health.
+
+## Completion criteria
+All new regression tests + full repo check pass; quota blocked/at-cap/under-cap
+behavior is pinned by tests; no accepted quality metric regresses; PR open with
+evidence; PC health after session no worse than before.
+
+## Final evidence
+Pending full `npm run check`. Focused suite: `node --test
+test/codex-work-quota.test.js test/master-coordinator.test.js` => 40 tests, 40
+PASS, 0 FAIL (incl. 11 new quota-module tests and 3 new coordinator gate
+tests). CLI smoke: no-ledger => allowed/exit 0; 2/3 Codex fixture => blocked
+"above the 30% daily cap", exit 1.
 
